# Compiled binaries. Each demo builds into its own bin/.
bin/

# Per-demo runtime state: PID files, logs, and the recorded mode. Deleted by
# `make clean`; never useful to anyone else.
.run/

# Captured profiles, traces and flame graphs.
#
# The binary captures are deliberately not committed: several megabytes each,
# specific to the machine and the Go version that produced them, and a stale one
# is worse than none — it invites you to explain numbers your code no longer
# produces. `make artifacts` recreates them in about two minutes.
#
# The directory structure and the small text summaries *are* committed. One
# directory per artifact kind, each with a .gitkeep, so the capture scripts have
# somewhere to write and a fresh clone shows what a capture produces. The .txt,
# .json and .md summaries are the fallback that survives a laptop swap: if no
# tool runs on stage, the numbers are still on disk.
artifacts/**
!artifacts/*/
!artifacts/**/.gitkeep
!artifacts/**/*.txt
!artifacts/**/*.json
!artifacts/**/*.md

# Ad-hoc captures that land outside artifacts/ when following the READMEs by hand.
*.pprof
*.folded
trace*.out
!scripts/*.sh

# go tool pprof and go tool trace scratch space
pprof/
